        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Your reasoning is exactly right, and it's the right reason: in a random draw, each of the 4 tiles is equally likely, so the shape you're most likely to draw is the one that occupies more of the bag.\n\nThat gives the probability:\n\n- **Round:** 3 out of 4 tiles → 3/4 = 0.75 (75%)\n- **Square:** 1 out of 4 tiles → 1/4 = 0.25 (25%)\n\nOne thing worth noticing: the *order* the tiles went into the bag doesn't matter at all for a random draw — only how many of each shape are in there. (If instead you'd drawn *twice without replacing*, the second draw would change, since the first tile would be gone from the bag.)\n\nLet you test the model directly:"
